   {
    "text": "Dear McQueen,\n\nI hope this note finds you in the best of health and spirits! I’ve been trying to figure out how to write a funny note to you, and I’ve been thinking about all the times you’ve been the best boss, the best friend, and the best… *everything*. But honestly, I’m still trying to wrap my head around how to make it funny without sounding too cheesy.\n\nLet me try to break it down mathematically. If I were to write this note, I’d start with a greeting that’s as funny as your personality. Maybe something like: “Hey McQueen, I’ve been trying to figure out how to write a funny note to you, and I’ve been thinking about all the times you’ve been the best boss, the best friend, and the best… everything. But honestly, I’m still trying to wrap my head around how to make it funny without sounding too cheesy.”\n\nThen, I’d include some mathematical notations to add a bit of humor. Maybe something like: “I’ve been trying to calculate the perfect amount of humor to include, and I’ve come up with a formula: H = (F + C) / (D + S), where F is the fun, C is the cleverness, D is the depth, and S is the sarcasm. But honestly, I’m still trying to figure out how to balance all of these variables.”\n\nI’ve also been thinking about the structure of the note. I want it to be clear and easy to read, but also a bit playful. Maybe I’ll add a line like: “I’ve been trying to write this note in a way that’s as funny as you are, and I think I’ve finally found the right balance.”\n\nP.P.S. If you ever need a funny note, just let me know—I’m always here to help!",
